==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*huspaz||derision, mockery}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{m|gem-pro|*hut-}}, {{m|gem-pro|*hūt-||to be naughty, be impudent}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*kūd-||to mock}}. Related to {{cog|ang|hyspan||to mock, scorn, deride}}, {{cog|ang|hūsc||mockery, derision, scorn, insult}}, {{cog|goh|hosc||vilification, ridicule, scorn}}.

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|head=hosp|m|hospas}}

# [[reproach]], [[contempt]], [[contumely]], [[insult]], [[blasphemy]]

====Declension====
{{ang-decl-noun-a-m|hosp|}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|ang|hospcwide}} m. insulting speech
* {{l|ang|hospettan}} to ridicule
* {{l|ang|hospspræc|hospsprǣċ}} f. jeer, taunt
* {{l|ang|hospul}} contemptible
* {{l|ang|hospword}} n. abusive language, contemptuous expression

